-- title:
--   Smoothness of the j-finite Igusa chart over k
-- statement:
--   Let $N \ge 1$ be a natural number, let $\ell$ be a prime not dividing $N$, let $k$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $\ell$, and let $\varphi$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, realised here as the subring [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) of $\mathbb{Q}$ consisting of those rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, into $k$. Write $A =$ `chartAlgFin N ℓ` for the $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$-subalgebra of the full modular function field of level $N$ consisting of all elements integral over the subalgebra generated by the modular invariant $j$ over $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, i.e. the integral closure of $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}[j]$ in that field. The theorem asserts that the second projection of the fibre product of $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)} \to A$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\varphi \colon \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}$, that is the base-changed morphism $\operatorname{Spec} A \times_{\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_{(\ell)}} \operatorname{Spec} k \to \operatorname{Spec} k$, is smooth of relative dimension $1$.
--
--   This is the good-reduction assertion of Igusa's theorem for the chart of the Igusa scheme where $j$ is finite: the characteristic-$\ell$ fibre of that chart is a smooth curve over $k$ when $\ell \nmid N$. It is one of the two affine charts feeding [`ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_residue`](thm.html#ModularCurve.IgusaScheme.smoothOfRelativeDimension_one_pullback_residue), where the charts are glued along the pushout presentation of the Igusa scheme.
